@startuml
title The oracle price is a median of medians
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

package "Stage 1 — inside every validator, every 3 s" {
  [Binance  w=3] as V1
  [OKX  w=2] as V2
  [Bybit  w=2] as V3
  [Kraken  w=1] as V4
  [KuCoin  w=1] as V5
  [Gate.io  w=1] as V6
  [MEXC  w=1] as V7
  [Hyperliquid spot  w=1] as V8
  [Weighted median\nof the included venues] as WM
  V1 --> WM
  V2 --> WM
  V3 --> WM
  V4 --> WM
  V5 --> WM
  V6 --> WM
  V7 --> WM
  V8 --> WM
}

note bottom of WM
  Inclusion depends on where the asset's
  spot liquidity actually is. HYPE-style
  assets exclude external venues until
  liquidity is sufficient; BTC-style assets
  exclude Hyperliquid spot.
end note

package "Stage 2 — across the validator set" {
  [Validator A submission] as A
  [Validator B submission] as B
  [Validator C submission] as C
  [Stake-weighted median] as SWM
  A --> SWM
  B --> SWM
  C --> SWM
}

WM --> A : each validator publishes\nits own number onchain
WM --> B
WM --> C

[Oracle price used by the clearinghouse] as OUT
SWM --> OUT

note right of OUT
  Two medians in series: one venue lying
  cannot move stage 1, and a minority of
  validators lying cannot move stage 2.
  Moving the result needs a majority of
  stake, not a majority of venues.
end note
@enduml
